contentText:
This year, Sony Music Publishing keeps topping its own record-breaking performances as measured by&nbsp; Billboard ’s 20-year-long history of ranking music publishers by market share for hit songs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

After scoring the highest-ever market share for the Hot 100 in the second quarter with&nbsp;37.32%, Sony has now become the first publisher ever to surpass the 40% market share milestone with&nbsp;42.86% in the just-completed third quarter, setting a new record&nbsp;for that chart.&nbsp;&nbsp;

